All implemented and verified — validator's 9/9 checks pass, plus the extras it doesn't cover.

**`app/auth.py`** — `require_api_key` now returns 401 when the `X-API-Key` header is missing or not in `VALID_API_KEYS`, otherwise returns the mapped username.

**`app/main.py`**:
- `GET /tasks` — optional `status` (validated as `TaskStatus`), `priority`, `assigned_to` filters, applied in sequence so they combine; then paginated via `page` (default 1) / `page_size` (default 20) slice.
- `POST /tasks` — `Depends(require_api_key)`, 404 if `project_id` not in `projects`, ID = `max(existing ids) + 1`, returns 201 with the created task.
- `PUT /tasks/{task_id}` — auth required, 404 if missing, partial update via `model_dump(exclude_unset=True)` so only sent fields change.
- `DELETE /tasks/{task_id}` — auth required, 404 if missing, returns 204 and removes the task.

Design note: ID generation is `max+1`, so a deleted ID can be reused later — fine for an in-memory list store, but if you want strictly monotonically unique IDs, a module-level counter would be needed. No test files existed; verified by running the challenge validator's own script in-process (9/9) plus a second process covering combined filters, page 2, and auth/404 on PUT/DELETE.
